  1180	# SECTION 7: 15% LABOR MARKUP FORMULA LINE
  1181	
  1182	## 7.1 Your Business Requirements
  1183	
  1184	**REQ-021: Implement 15% labor markup formula line (cost-only, no revenue) (ACCOMMODATE)**
  1185	
  1186	KBM Hogue has a unique and powerful pricing discipline mechanism: a 15% labor markup formula line that automatically appears on every sales order with labor. This is a cost-only line (no revenue), which means it takes 15% of the cost of external labor and further reduces project GP. It's a behavioral forcing function—a built-in contingency that prevents teams from underpricing labor and ensures appropriate margins.
  1187	
  1188	**REQ-022: Apply markup only to external labor (not all labor types) (ACCOMMODATE)**
  1189	
  1190	The markup doesn't apply to all labor. It applies specifically to external labor (warehouse labor, installation labor from contractors). Internal PM labor and design labor are excluded. The system identifies which labor should trigger the formula by checking line codes—lines coded as "external labor" trigger the formula calculation.
  1191	
  1192	**REQ-023: Position formula line at bottom (not top), make uneditable and non-printing (ACCOMMODATE)**
  1193	
  1194	In Core, the formula line appears as line 1, which frustrates Kipp (IT Specialist) because customer proposals start at line 2 instead of line 1. In NetSuite, the formula line must be positioned at the absolute bottom of the order (after all normal lines), be completely uneditable (can't be manually changed), and not print on customer proposals (internal only). It must remain dynamic—recalculating whenever labor lines are added or removed.
  1195	
  1196	**Requirements Classification:**
  1197	- Type: Functional - Pricing discipline mechanism
  1198	- Priority: Must-Have (critical to pricing discipline according to leadership)
  1199	- Users Impacted: Account managers (automatic calculation), finance team (GP impact), leadership (pricing discipline)
  1200	- Business Impact: Enforces margin discipline, prevents labor underpricing, behavioral forcing function
  1201	
  1202	---
  1203	
  1204	## 7.2 Current State Process
  1205	
  1206	**PROCESS:** 15% Labor Markup in Core (Current State - Problematic)
  1207	
  1208	**TRIGGER:** New sales order created with labor line
  1209	
  1210	**CURRENT STEPS:**
  1211	1. Account manager creates sales order with labor lines
  1212	2. Automatically, Core pulls in a line "KPMG 15%"
  1213	3. Line is line 1 (first line on order)
  1214	4. Formula calculates 15% of external labor cost, displays negative cost
  1215	5. Project GP reduced by 15% of labor cost (behavioral enforcement)
  1216	6. When proposal printed, line 1 is the formula line, so proposal shows line numbers starting at 2
  1217	7. Kipp hates this: "My biggest gripe about that is that it's always line one. So any time you issue a proposal with line numbers it starts at two. Somebody with OCD... I will murder this thing."
  1218	
  1219	**CURRENT WORKAROUNDS:**
  1220	- Some users manually delete and re-add the line (but it comes back)
  1221	- Some reorder lines manually (cumbersome process)
  1222	- Proposals printed with awkward line numbering (line 2-37 instead of 1-36)
