  1938	
  1939	## 9.8 Implementation Considerations
  1940	
  1941	- **Device Management:** Plan for tablet/phone procurement, OS standardization, security policies
  1942	- **Network Requirements:** Most sites will have some connectivity; offline mode handles gaps
  1943	- **User Training:** All PMs and contractors need training on app features, check-in, photo capture, time entry
  1944	- **Contractor Adoption:** Some contractors may resist new system; clear communication and support needed
  1945	- **Photo Storage:** Digital photos from all projects can require significant storage; cloud storage strategy important
  1946	- **GPS Accuracy:** Define acceptable distance tolerance for check-in (suggest 0.25 miles / ~400 meters)
  1947	- **Support Process:** Plan for technical support when users have app issues in field
  1948	- **Hardware Security:** Tablets/phones will contain project information; security policies for device loss/theft
  1949	- **Data Backup:** Regular backups of field app data to prevent loss
  1950	- **Performance:** App must be responsive and reliable; slow or crashed app hurts field productivity
  1951	- **Phased Rollout:** Consider piloting with one PM team before full deployment
