  1754	The dashboard is filtered by date—showing today's work prominently, with ability to view upcoming days. Users can see at a glance what's scheduled, prioritize the order, and quickly navigate between multiple events without needing email or paper.
  1755	
  1756	**Check-In with Geological Stamping:**
  1757	
  1758	When a PM or contractor arrives at the job site, they tap "Check In" in the app. The app captures their GPS location (geological stamp) and records the time. This check-in serves multiple purposes:
  1759	- Accountability: Management can verify the resource was actually on-site at the claimed time
  1760	- Compliance: Provides evidence of site visit for project records
  1761	- Dispute resolution: If questions arise about whether work was performed, check-in proves presence
  1762	- Time tracking: Check-in time can auto-populate time entry (though manual time entry may still be needed for multiple resources)
  1763	
  1764	Geological stamping is proven industry practice and valued by managers for oversight and quality assurance.
  1765	
  1766	**Photo Capture and Documentation:**
  1767	
  1768	Rather than using separate camera apps or PlanGrid, field users take photos directly in the Field Service app. Photos are automatically associated with the work order event and stored in NetSuite with complete metadata (date, time, location, user). Users can:
  1769	- Take photos from items list (progress on delivery)
  1770	- Take photos for punch items (documentation of issues)
  1771	- Upload existing photos/documents
  1772	- Attach files for specific line items
  1773	
  1774	**Signature Collection:**
  1775	
  1776	If client sign-off is needed (delivery completion, punch list acceptance), users can collect signatures directly in the app. Signature canvas displays on tablet, user signs, signature is captured digitally and stored with the event. This eliminates need for separate signature apps and paper forms.
  1777	
  1778	**Multi-Resource Time Entry:**
  1779	
  1780	If five workers are on a single work order event, users enter time once specifying "5 people worked 4 hours" and the system creates time entries for all resources. This simplifies labor-intensive time entry and prevents missed entries. Users can also add temporary resources dynamically if additional support is needed during the day.
  1781	
  1782	**Offline Mode (Previously Discussed):**
  1783	
  1784	As noted in Section 8, the app works offline: download work info in morning, work all day without connectivity, sync when back online.
  1785	
  1786	This approach has been successfully deployed across contract furniture dealers and represents best practice for field operations and mobile workforce management.
